Additional Use Grant: You may make Production use of the Licensed Work,
                      provided that You are an Eligible User and Your use
                      does not include a Hosted Offering.

                      1. Eligible Users

                      An "Eligible User" is any of the following:

                      (a) an individual using the Licensed Work on their own
                          behalf, and not on behalf of or for the benefit of
                          an Organisation;

                      (b) an Organisation whose Annual Revenue is less than
                          USD 10,000,000 (ten million US dollars);

                      (c) any person or Organisation using the Licensed Work
                          solely to document a Public Open Source Project;

                      (d) an accredited educational institution, using the
                          Licensed Work solely for teaching or academic
                          research, and not for its administrative or
                          commercial operations; or

                      (e) any Organisation, during one evaluation period of
                          up to ninety (90) days starting on the date it
                          first makes Production use of any version of the
                          Licensed Work, or any longer period agreed in
                          writing by the Licensor. Each Organisation,
                          including all of its Affiliates, has one
                          evaluation period in total, across all versions of
                          the Licensed Work. Upgrading to a new version,
                          reinstalling the Licensed Work, creating another
                          catalog, or a change in the Organisation's
                          Affiliates does not start a new evaluation period.

                      2. Crossing the threshold

                      An Organisation that is an Eligible User under (b)
                      remains one until ninety (90) days after the end of
                      the first financial year for which its Annual Revenue
                      equals or exceeds USD 10,000,000.

                      3. Service providers

                      Where You use the Licensed Work to provide services to
                      a client (for example, as a consultant, contractor or
                      agency) and that use is for the client's benefit,
                      Your use is permitted if the client is an Eligible
                      User or holds a commercial license from the Licensor
                      that covers that use.

                      4. Cure period

                      If You stop being an Eligible User, or learn that
                      Your use is not permitted by this Additional Use
                      Grant, You may continue to use the Licensed Work for
                      thirty (30) days in order to obtain a commercial
                      license or stop that use (the "Cure Period"). Such
                      continued use during the Cure Period is permitted
                      Production use under this Additional Use Grant, is
                      not a use in violation of this License, and Your
                      rights under this License will not terminate during
                      the Cure Period for that reason.

                      5. Definitions

                      "Production use" includes any use of a catalog built
                      with the Licensed Work that an Organisation's
                      employees, contractors or automated systems
                      (including AI agents) rely on to document, discover,
                      understand or govern its software systems, whether
                      that catalog is available internally, privately or
                      publicly, and use of the Licensed Work in continuous
                      integration or deployment pipelines to build, update
                      or validate such a catalog. For the avoidance of
                      doubt, use that is internal to an Organisation can be
                      Production use.

                      "Organisation" means a legal entity together with all
                      of its Affiliates. "Affiliate" means any entity that
                      directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by, or
                      is under common control with that legal entity, where
                      "control" means ownership of more than fifty percent
                      (50%) of the voting interests of the entity. For a
                      government or public-sector body, the Organisation is
                      that body (for example, a ministry, department,
                      agency or local authority), and not the wider
                      government of which it forms part.

                      "Annual Revenue" means the total consolidated gross
                      revenue of the Organisation for its most recently
                      completed financial year or, if it has not yet
                      completed a financial year, its reasonably projected
                      revenue for its first financial year. For a
                      government or public-sector body, charity or
                      non-profit organisation, it means the greater of its
                      total income (including grants and donations) and its
                      total annual budget for that financial year. Amounts
                      in other currencies are converted to US dollars at
                      the average exchange rate for that financial year.

                      "Public Open Source Project" means a software project
                      whose source code is publicly available under a
                      license approved by the Open Source Initiative, where
                      the catalog documents only that project.

                      "Hosted Offering" means using the Licensed Work to
                      provide third parties with access to the Licensed
                      Work, or to its functionality, as a hosted or managed
                      service, whether or not for a fee. The following are
                      not Hosted Offerings: publishing a catalog that
                      documents Your own software systems, including making
                      it publicly accessible; and hosting a catalog on
                      behalf of a client, where the catalog documents that
                      client's software systems and the client is an
                      Eligible User or holds a commercial license from the
                      Licensor that covers that use.

                      All other Production use requires a commercial
                      license from the Licensor. Interpretive guidance is
                      published at https://www.eventcatalog.dev/license-faq.
                      Guidance for a version of the Licensed Work will not
                      be changed to further restrict use of that version.
